  "properties": {
    "title": "Vector Mosaicking with GeoServer",
    "description": "The vector mosaic datastore is a new feature in GeoServer that allows indexing many smaller vector stores (e.g., shapefiles, FlatGeoBuf, Geoparquet) and serving them as a single, seamless data source. This has the advantage of cost savings when dealing with very large amounts of data in the cloud, as blob storage bills at a fraction of an equivalent database. It is also faster for specific use cases, e.g, when extracting a single file from a large collection and rendering it fully (e.g. tractor tracks in a precision farming application).\r\n\r\nAttend this presentation to learn more about vector mosaic setup, tuning, migration from large relations databases, and real world experiences.",
